course: french
lesson: 26
title: Plurals: les, des and silent s
level: primary-4
stars: 1
explain: In French you usually make a noun plural with an s, just like English, but there is a twist: the s is almost always silent, so le chat and les chats sound the same at the end.
explain: You hear the plural in the little word in front instead: le chat sounds "luh SHA", les chats sounds "lay SHA", and des chats, "day SHA", means "some cats".
explain: Picture a French farm: un cheval in the field becomes des chevaux, un oiseau on the roof becomes des oiseaux, and you cannot see un œil but deux yeux.
explain: The silent s wakes up before a vowel and is said as z, so les enfants sounds "lay-zahn-FAHN" - a little bridge between the two words.
explain: When the noun goes plural, everything travelling with it goes plural too: les yeux bleus, les chevaux sont dans le champ.
fact: The plural s is usually silent but must be written: le chat ("luh SHA"), les chats ("lay SHA").
fact: Des is the plural of un and une: un livre, des livres; une pomme, des pommes. French keeps des where English often says nothing.
fact: Words ending in -eau and -eu usually add x, not s: des gâteaux, des bateaux, des oiseaux, des jeux.
fact: Words ending in -al usually change to -aux: un animal, des animaux; un cheval, des chevaux; un journal, des journaux.
fact: Nouns already ending in s, x or z do not change: le nez, les nez; la souris, les souris; le prix, les prix.
fact: Before a vowel the silent s of les and des is said as z: les enfants ("lay-zahn-FAHN"), des oranges.
fact: An adjective goes plural with its noun: les yeux bleus, les chats noirs.
fact: Œil (eye) has a completely different plural: un œil, deux yeux, like mouse and mice in English.
fact: A plural noun takes a plural verb: le cheval est, but les chevaux sont.
fact: After pas, des becomes de: J'ai des bonbons, but Je n'ai pas de bonbons.
fact: In des jeux vidéo, jeu takes x and vidéo usually stays without s.
exercise: Oliver writes "les chat". What is right? | les chats | les chat | le chats | les chates
exercise: How can you hear that "les chats" is plural? | From les, which sounds "lay" | From the s, which you can hear | From the cats all miaowing twice | You can't, it sounds just like le chat
exercise: What is the plural of un chat? | des chats | uns chats | des chat | les chat
exercise: Leo writes "deux gâteaus". What is right? | deux gâteaux | deux gâteaus | deux gâteauxs | deux gâtaux
exercise: Grace writes "les animals". What is right? | les animaux | les animals | les animales | les animauxs
exercise: Which is the plural of un journal? | des journaux | des journals | des journales | des journauxs
exercise: Ethan writes about two noses. Which is right? | les nez | les nezs | les nezes | les neux
exercise: Which noun stays the same in the plural? | la souris | le chat | le jeu | le cheval
exercise: How does les enfants sound? | "lay-zahn-FAHN", with a z sound | "lay-ahn-FAHN", with a gap | "less-ahn-FAHNTS", every letter | "luh-zahn-FAHN", like one child
exercise: Jayden writes "les yeux bleu". What is right? | les yeux bleus | les yeux bleu | les yeuxs bleus | les œils bleus
exercise: Mason writes "deux œils". What is right? | deux yeux | deux œils | deux œilx | deux yeuxs
exercise: Freya says "Les cheval sont dans le champ." What is right? | Les chevaux sont dans le champ | Les chevals sont dans le champ | Les chevaux est dans le champ | Le chevaux sont dans le champ
exercise: How do you say "I don't have any sweets"? | Je n'ai pas de bonbons | Je n'ai pas des bonbons | Je n'ai des bonbons pas | Je ai pas de bonbons
exercise: Hannah writes "deux jeus". What is right? | deux jeux | deux jeus | deux jeues | deux jeuxs
exercise: Which is the usual spelling of video games? | des jeux vidéo | des jeus vidéos | des jeux vidéos | des jeu vidéo
test: Your mate goes, "Bruv, you can't even hear the s, so why bother writing it?" What's the answer? | Spelling still needs it, and les tells the ear it's plural | He's right, French people never write it | The s is said loudly in posh French | The s is only written on Mondays
test: Ava from Cork says, "Sure des is just 'some' with a posh hat, I can leave it out." Can she? | No, French keeps des where English drops "some" | Yes, des is just for posh people | Yes, French drops des like English | No, but only in questions
test: ★ Why do bateau, oiseau and jeu all end in x in the plural? | Words ending in -eau and -eu take x | They are all things that move fast | They are all masculine words | It's a random spelling mistake
test: ★ A boy says "un animal, deux animaux" and his little sister asks why it sounds different. What changed? | -al became -aux, said "oh" | Nothing, they sound the same | The s at the end is now said aloud | The word got a new, feminine gender
test: Gran from Somerset reads "les souris" and goes, "Proper job, but where's the s, my lover? Should be les souriss." What is true? | Souris already ends in s, so it doesn't change | She's right, you add another s | It should be les sourix | It should be les souriz
test: A cartoon pirate shouts "J'ai deux œils !" What should he shout? | J'ai deux yeux ! | J'ai deux œils ! | J'ai deux œilx ! | J'ai deux yeuxs !
test: ★★★ How many of these plurals are spelled right? les chevaux, les gâteaus, les nez, les jeux, les animals | Three | Two | Four | Five
test: What would happen if a French child read "les amis" with no z sound? | It would sound choppy, but people would understand | It would mean only one friend | It would mean "the enemies" | Nobody would notice, there's never a z sound
test: ★ Kai from Auckland writes "Je n'ai pas des frères." His mate says, "Yeah nah, sounds sweet as." (yeah nah = no) Fix it. | Je n'ai pas de frères | Je n'ai pas des frère | Je n'ai pas les frères | Je n'ai des frères pas
test: ★★★ Every word must agree. Which sentence is all right? | Les chats noirs sont dans les jardins | Les chats noir sont dans les jardins | Les chats noirs est dans les jardins | Le chats noirs sont dans les jardin
test: Your cousin texts "les chevals sont trop mignons lol" (mignons = cute). What's wrong? | It should be chevaux: -al becomes -aux | Nothing, chevals is right | It should be cheveaux with an e | It should be les cheval, no s
exam: Identify the plural form of the noun "gâteau" in accordance with the rules of French orthography. | gâteaux | gâteaus | gâteauxs | gâtaux
exam: Ascertain the plural form corresponding to the singular noun "œil". | yeux | œils | œilx | œiles
exam: Determine the form assumed by the article des subsequent to the negative particle pas. | de | des | les | aucun
exam: State the manner in which the final consonant of "les" is pronounced when it precedes a word commencing with a vowel. | As the sound z | As the sound s, as in English | It remains entirely silent | As the sound t, sharply
